    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, my tomato plants are acting weird. the leaves at the bottom are turning yellow but the ones at the top look okay. what do you think is going on and how can i fix the soil?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing lower leaves on tomatoes usually signals a nitrogen deficiency, since the plant moves available nitrogen to the newer top growth. It can also be caused by overwatering, which leaches nutrients and suffocates roots. To fix the soil, water less frequently and apply a balanced fertilizer like compost tea or a 5-5-5 granular feed, ensuring it’s worked into the top few inches. If the yellowing spreads upward, check for root rot or adjust pH to 6.0–6.8 for better nutrient uptake.",
